    "result_text": "All tests pass. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required de-duplicating a computed `customerCode` when it collides with an existing owner's code, appending `-<n>` with the smallest `n >= 2`.\n\nThe `existing` collection was already plumbed into `CustomerCode.of(...)` but unused. I kept structural impact minimal:\n\n- **`of` changed by 2 lines**, CC stays 1 \u2014 it computes the base code, then delegates to a new helper.\n- **Added `dedupe(...)`** as a small cohesive unit (CC 2) that collects existing codes into a `Set` and increments `n` from 2 until the candidate is free.\n\nNo other methods, classes, or files were touched. `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodesStayUnique` and the full suite are green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
